  "notes": [
    "added by ADR 0009 Amendment 2 (2026-08-16), which rules that a volatile dependency can reach stale and only via a probe's Drift",
    "The TTL is never advanced here: the whole point is that the window is still open and the probe still decided the edge. The sibling fixtures volatile-external-dep and volatile-external-dep-probed cover the TTL-expiry path.",
    "Trust classes bound how strongly FreshDAG may assert something is unchanged; they say nothing about its ability to observe that something changed. Reporting likely-valid on an input that demonstrably moved would be invariant #7's harm arriving from the opposite direction, and invariant #15 settles it: correctness beats cache hit rate.",
    "The first implementation of the ADR 0009 Amendment 1 code motion decided volatile edges in full before arbitration, so this scenario would have reported likely-valid -- strictly worse drift detection than the defect it repaired. This fixture exists to make that regression impossible to reintroduce silently."
  ]
